1
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,310
Is that Estermont?

2
00:03:17,030 --> 00:03:18,810
Tarth, Ser Jaime.

3
00:03:21,310 --> 00:03:22,830
The Sapphire Isle.

4
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:29,160
Why are we on a merchant ship?

5
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:31,200
Why no Lannister sails?

6
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:35,650
This ship's sailing to Oldtown.

7
00:03:35,650 --> 00:03:38,120
We'll get off earlier, not far from Sunspear.

8
00:03:38,350 --> 00:03:40,710
Row ourselves to the Dornish shores in the night.

9
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:43,830
You ever been to Dorne?

10
00:03:44,210 --> 00:03:45,760
- No. - I have.

11
00:03:45,990 --> 00:03:47,580
The Dornish are crazy.

12
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:50,330
All they want to do is fight and fuck, fuck and fight.

13
00:03:50,330 --> 00:03:52,160
You should be happy to go back.

14
00:03:54,210 --> 00:03:55,600
There's nothing like a good fight

15
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:57,540
to get you in the mood for fucking.

16
00:03:57,730 --> 00:03:59,990
And there's nothing like a fuck-mad Dornish girl

17
00:04:00,070 --> 00:04:02,350
to clear your head for the next fight.

18
00:04:02,570 --> 00:04:04,420
It's how the two work together.

19
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:06,810
Now we're gonna be doing a lot of fighting, I am sure.

20
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:08,220
Well, I am.

21
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:11,280
But I don't imagine we'll get to stick around for the rest.

22
00:04:11,310 --> 00:04:13,080
Not after we've kidnapped their princess.

23
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:15,200
We are not kidnapping their princess.

24
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:18,240
We are rescuing my niece, bringing her back to her family,

25
00:04:18,730 --> 00:04:19,870
Your niece?

26
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,150
I've been doing this sort of thing a long time.

27
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:31,410
I'm good at it.

28
00:04:31,410 --> 00:04:33,230
- That's why you're here. - I know.

29
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:34,470
Why are you here?

30
00:04:34,470 --> 00:04:37,200
Why not send 40 of me? Or an army?

31
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:39,390
Unlike most folks, you've actually got one.

32
00:04:39,390 --> 00:04:41,430
Because I don't want to start a war.

33
00:04:43,130 --> 00:04:45,740
That still doesn't explain what you're doing here.

34
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:49,770
It has to be me.

35
00:04:53,030 --> 00:04:55,170
If I'm putting something like this together,

36
00:04:55,470 --> 00:04:56,710
a one-handed man

37
00:04:56,710 --> 00:04:57,520
who happens to be

38
00:04:57,520 --> 00:05:00,240
one of the most recognizable faces in Westeros is not...

39
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:01,750
It has to be me.

40
00:05:07,610 --> 00:05:09,590
You set your brother free, didn't you?

41
00:05:11,660 --> 00:05:13,530
I'll bet your sister didn't like that.

42
00:05:15,580 --> 00:05:17,410
Varys set him free.

43
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:22,640
Well...

44
00:05:24,610 --> 00:05:28,400
if you ever see the wee fucker, give him my regards.

45
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:34,310
He murdered my father.

46
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:39,880
If I ever see him, I'll split him in two.

47
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:43,340
And then I'll give him your regards.

48
00:05:49,790 --> 00:05:54,210
The Iron Bank has called in one tenth of the Crown's debts.

49
00:05:54,540 --> 00:05:56,850
Given the expense of rebuilding the royal fleet...

50
00:05:56,850 --> 00:05:58,700
How much can the Crown afford?

51
00:05:58,850 --> 00:06:02,070
With winter coming, half what they ask.

52
00:06:02,650 --> 00:06:05,350
- Less? - You're the Master of Coin.

53
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:06,620
How do we pay them?

54
00:06:06,630 --> 00:06:09,360
House Tyrell could front the gold and the...

55
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:11,170
the Crown would pay us back in time,

56
00:06:11,180 --> 00:06:13,650
or I'd have words with my daughter.

57
00:06:19,320 --> 00:06:21,320
You've already given us too much.

58
00:06:22,770 --> 00:06:25,830
No, we must arrange better terms with the Iron Bank.

59
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:27,960
- Absolutely. - In person.

60
00:06:30,260 --> 00:06:31,060
Me?

61
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:33,000
We must send an envoy to the Iron Bank,

62
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:36,690
someone of importance to show these bankers our respect.

63
00:06:36,690 --> 00:06:37,910
As the King's Master of Coin,

64
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:39,770
I can think of no one more qualified.

65
00:06:39,770 --> 00:06:41,490
I would be honored, Your Grace.

66
00:06:41,490 --> 00:06:42,780
The King has expressed concern

67
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:45,590
about his father-in-law's safety on this voyage.

68
00:06:49,030 --> 00:06:53,060
He's ordered Ser Meryn to personally lead your escort.

69
00:06:55,150 --> 00:06:57,060
My very own Kingsguard?

70
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:59,420
- Please express my... - Safe travels, Lord Tyrell.

71
00:06:59,970 --> 00:07:01,600
Of course, of course,

72
00:07:01,810 --> 00:07:05,130
I'll give your regards to the Titan of Braavos.

73
00:07:14,180 --> 00:07:17,350
The Small Council grows smaller and smaller.

74
00:07:17,350 --> 00:07:19,100
Not small enough.

75
00:07:29,830 --> 00:07:32,280
May I offer you some wine, Your Holiness?

76
00:07:33,150 --> 00:07:34,120
No.

77
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:40,750
The old High Septon would have asked the vintage.

78
00:07:40,750 --> 00:07:44,130
I could say that our minds are temples to the Seven

79
00:07:44,140 --> 00:07:46,000
and should be kept pure.

80
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:48,120
But the truth is

81
00:07:48,370 --> 00:07:50,370
I don't like the taste.

82
00:07:53,070 --> 00:07:54,520
How may I serve?

83
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:59,000
All over Westeros we hear of septs being burned,

84
00:07:59,260 --> 00:08:01,580
silent sisters raped,

85
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:04,980
bodies of holy men piled in the streets.

86
00:08:04,980 --> 00:08:07,560
Wars teach people to obey the sword,

87
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:08,630
not the Gods.

88
00:08:08,630 --> 00:08:11,070
Perhaps the Gods need a sword of their own.

89
00:08:11,950 --> 00:08:13,550
In the days before the Targaryens,

90
00:08:13,550 --> 00:08:17,030
the Faith Militant dispensed the justice of the Seven.

91
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:21,090
Well, the Faith Militant was disarmed more than two centuries ago.

92
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:24,890
If I explain their holy purpose to my son the king,

93
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:26,790
I have no doubt he will sign

94
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:29,900
a decree arming the believers you find worthy.

95
00:08:30,140 --> 00:08:34,050
An army that defends the bodies and souls of the common people.

96
00:08:34,050 --> 00:08:37,070
An army and service to the Gods themselves.

97
00:08:37,070 --> 00:08:38,760
And to you, of course.

98
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:41,340
As the chosen representative of the Seven.

99
00:08:41,340 --> 00:08:43,700
An honor I've never expected.

100
00:08:44,180 --> 00:08:46,020
Or, indeed, ever wished for.

101
00:08:46,020 --> 00:08:47,800
Which is why you were chosen.

102
00:08:49,870 --> 00:08:52,280
You and I both know how the world works.

103
00:08:52,430 --> 00:08:54,450
Too often the wicked are the wealthiest,

104
00:08:54,450 --> 00:08:56,200
beyond the reach of justice.

105
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:59,970
The king himself cannot always punish those who deserve it most.

106
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:02,760
All sinners are equal before the Gods.

107
00:09:07,450 --> 00:09:11,810
What would you say if I told you of a great sinner in our very midst?

108
00:09:11,990 --> 00:09:14,670
Shielded by gold and privilege.

109
00:09:16,970 --> 00:09:19,180
May the Father judge him justly.

110
00:09:58,210 --> 00:10:00,170
Help me! Help me!

111
00:10:30,730 --> 00:10:33,470
This is Lord Petyr Baelish's establishment.

112
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:45,840
Cocksucker!

113
00:10:47,190 --> 00:10:49,000
Boy fucker!

114
00:10:49,550 --> 00:10:51,840
You buggering filth!

115
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:55,930
There's a special place in the Seven Hells for your kind.

116
00:10:55,930 --> 00:10:58,850
Please, please, I'll pay!

117
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:00,580
I'll pay all of you.

118
00:11:01,330 --> 00:11:02,770
Yes, you will!

119
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:39,480
Seize him.

120
00:11:41,870 --> 00:11:42,540
Get your hands off me.

121
00:11:42,540 --> 00:11:44,330
Ser Loras of House Tyrell,

122
00:11:44,340 --> 00:11:46,490
you have broken the laws of Gods and men.

123
00:11:47,990 --> 00:11:49,050
Who do you think you are?

124
00:11:50,510 --> 00:11:51,750
Justice.

125
00:11:58,530 --> 00:12:00,240
Why is my brother in a cell?

126
00:12:00,990 --> 00:12:02,370
I--I don't know.

127
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:05,120
I--I didn't order it.

128
00:12:05,230 --> 00:12:06,790
We both know who did.

129
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:10,620
You told me she was returning to Casterly Rock.

130
00:12:12,090 --> 00:12:13,860
Are you saying my mother is behind this?

131
00:12:13,930 --> 00:12:16,330
She's jealous you're not hers anymore.

132
00:12:16,330 --> 00:12:19,350
Arresting my brother is her revenge.

133
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:21,130
Aren't you and mother getting along?

134
00:12:27,180 --> 00:12:30,940
Oh, my sweet, sweet King.

135
00:12:32,790 --> 00:12:35,750
Do you have any affection for me at all?

136
00:12:37,410 --> 00:12:39,140
Of course I do.

137
00:12:39,830 --> 00:12:41,240
You're my Queen.

138
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:46,100
I can't bear to think of my brother locked away in some grimy cell.

139
00:12:48,660 --> 00:12:50,170
I'll set him free for you.

140
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:52,030
Do you promise?

141
00:12:59,350 --> 00:13:02,210
I demand that Ser Loras be freed now!

142
00:13:02,250 --> 00:13:03,550
Did I arrest him?

143
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:06,680
Well, no...

144
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:09,890
But you armed the Faith Militant.

145
00:13:09,890 --> 00:13:12,410
You gave the High Sparrow an army.

146
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:14,090
I did.

147
00:13:15,990 --> 00:13:18,620
And your wife has every right to criticize.

148
00:13:20,190 --> 00:13:22,590
We can't allow fanatics to arrest the Queen's brother

149
00:13:22,590 --> 00:13:24,680
no matter his perversions.

150
00:13:25,690 --> 00:13:26,800
Then...

151
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:31,190
can I tell Margaery you'll have Ser Loras released?

152
00:13:31,190 --> 00:13:33,600
I told you, I am not holding Ser Loras.

153
00:13:34,690 --> 00:13:35,910
You're the King.

154
00:13:35,910 --> 00:13:37,640
I'm sure if you speak to the High Sparrow,

155
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:39,340
he'll release the poor boy.

156
00:13:45,150 --> 00:13:46,160
Halt!

157
00:14:09,950 --> 00:14:13,110
His Holiness is praying. He will not be disturbed.

158
00:14:14,690 --> 00:14:17,680
Give the order and we'll clear out this rabble.

159
00:14:19,590 --> 00:14:23,860
You mean, kill them? Here, in the sept?

160
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,580
You'd be sending them to meet the Gods that they love.

161
00:14:30,490 --> 00:14:31,920
Bastard!

162
00:14:33,190 --> 00:14:34,840
You're an abomination!

163
00:14:39,910 --> 00:14:41,470
Born of sin!

164
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:44,320
Filthy bastard!

165
00:14:49,150 --> 00:14:50,500
We'll find another way.

166
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:54,820
Abomination!

167
00:15:00,660 --> 00:15:01,650
My Queen?

168
00:15:07,640 --> 00:15:10,430
There was no way to free Ser Loras without violence.

169
00:15:13,470 --> 00:15:15,200
You're the King of the Andals,

170
00:15:16,010 --> 00:15:19,390
the Lord of the Seven Kingdoms, the Protector of the Realm.

171
00:15:19,870 --> 00:15:22,930
And you let a band of fanatics imprison your brother by law.

172
00:15:24,740 --> 00:15:27,580
- I'm going to speak with the High Sparrow. - Are you? When?

173
00:15:29,890 --> 00:15:31,680
- I--I don't know. - You don't know?

174
00:15:32,370 --> 00:15:34,480
He was praying just now.

175
00:15:37,930 --> 00:15:39,740
I have to send word to Grandmother.

176
00:15:40,790 --> 00:15:42,320
Will you come back later?

177
00:15:44,790 --> 00:15:47,140
I need to be with my family, Your Grace.

178
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:50,010
Of course.

179
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:54,850
You think highly of this boy?

180
00:15:55,750 --> 00:15:56,410
Good.

181
00:15:56,410 --> 00:15:58,320
Lord Commander of the Night's Watch.

182
00:15:58,330 --> 00:16:00,940
And a bastard by some tavern slut.

183
00:16:00,950 --> 00:16:03,810
Perhaps, but that wasn't Ned Stark's way.

184
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:09,680
I should have given you a son.

185
00:16:11,940 --> 00:16:14,270
- Not your fault. - Whose, then?

186
00:16:15,700 --> 00:16:17,930
I gave you nothing but weakness

187
00:16:21,070 --> 00:16:22,570
and deformity.

188
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:26,470
Those scars mean nothing to the Lord of Light.

189
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:27,540
My Lady.

190
00:16:28,610 --> 00:16:30,630
Her father is the Lord's chosen King,

191
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:33,370
and her father's blood runs through her veins.

192
00:16:43,070 --> 00:16:45,040
You march on Winterfell soon?

193
00:16:45,180 --> 00:16:46,300
We must

194
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:48,580
to beat the snows.

195
00:16:49,860 --> 00:16:53,840
Once before, you put your faith in Ser Davos and left me behind.

196
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:58,920
I hope you won't make that mistake again.

197
00:16:58,920 --> 00:16:59,930
I won't.

198
00:17:03,490 --> 00:17:04,770
I need you.

199
00:17:04,900 --> 00:17:07,110
You only need faith, my King.

200
00:17:12,060 --> 00:17:13,960
And you, my Lady, what do you need?

201
00:17:15,760 --> 00:17:17,280
To serve my Lord.

202
00:17:22,330 --> 00:17:23,650
Lord Ashford.

203
00:17:29,870 --> 00:17:31,470
Lady Caulfield.

204
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:35,940
Lord Smallwood.

205
00:17:36,740 --> 00:17:38,120
I've never even heard of these people.

206
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:40,130
They haven't heard of you, either.

207
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:42,940
But we need men and they have some.

208
00:17:45,590 --> 00:17:48,590
How many men does this Lord Mayzen have to send us?

209
00:17:48,660 --> 00:17:50,600
More than Lord Wibberley.

210
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:05,900
- Not him. - I know.

211
00:18:05,900 --> 00:18:08,860
I'm sorry, but we need men and supplies

212
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:10,410
and Roose Bolton is the Warden of...

213
00:18:10,420 --> 00:18:11,640
He murdered my brother.

214
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:14,500
We swore to be the Watchers on the Wall.

215
00:18:15,270 --> 00:18:17,580
We can't watch the Wall with 50 men.

216
00:18:18,950 --> 00:18:20,360
And we can't get more men

217
00:18:20,370 --> 00:18:22,880
without help from the Warden of the North.

218
00:18:45,860 --> 00:18:47,330
Apologies, my Lady.

219
00:18:59,910 --> 00:19:01,270
Lord Commander.

220
00:19:02,120 --> 00:19:03,360
How can I help you?

221
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:06,150
Come with us when we ride south.

222
00:19:06,510 --> 00:19:08,830
None of us know the castle as well as you do.

223
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:12,940
Its hidden tunnels, its weaknesses, its people.

224
00:19:14,470 --> 00:19:16,690
Winterfell was your home once.

225
00:19:18,210 --> 00:19:20,770
Don't you want to chase the rats out of it?

226
00:19:23,390 --> 00:19:25,630
Castle Black is my home now.

227
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:29,530
The Night's Watch take no part in the wars of the Seven Kingdoms.

228
00:19:29,530 --> 00:19:31,030
There's only one war.

229
00:19:31,780 --> 00:19:33,840
Life against death.

230
00:19:35,730 --> 00:19:36,820
Come.

231
00:19:37,040 --> 00:19:38,990
Let me show what you're fighting for.

232
00:19:38,990 --> 00:19:41,050
You're gonna show me some vision in the fire.

233
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:43,300
Forgive me, my Lady,

234
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:45,250
I don't trust in visions.

235
00:19:46,610 --> 00:19:47,900
No visions.

236
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:49,590
No magic.

237
00:19:50,470 --> 00:19:51,790
Just life.

238
00:20:12,230 --> 00:20:14,060
Do you feel my heart beating?

239
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:18,660
There's power in you.

240
00:20:19,060 --> 00:20:23,010
You resist it, and that's your mistake. Embrace it.

241
00:20:34,010 --> 00:20:36,940
The Lord of Light made us male and female.

242
00:20:37,670 --> 00:20:39,880
Two parts of a greater whole.

243
00:20:41,120 --> 00:20:43,770
In our joining, there's power.

244
00:20:45,170 --> 00:20:47,000
Power to make life,

245
00:20:47,520 --> 00:20:49,390
power to make light,

246
00:20:50,210 --> 00:20:52,480
and power to cast shadows.

247
00:20:53,110 --> 00:20:56,130
I don't think Stannis would like that very much.

248
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:58,500
Then we shouldn't tell him.

249
00:20:59,980 --> 00:21:01,310
I can't.

250
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:03,050
Why?

251
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:05,250
I swore a vow.

252
00:21:07,700 --> 00:21:09,030
I loved another.

253
00:21:09,870 --> 00:21:11,890
The dead don't need lovers.

254
00:21:12,280 --> 00:21:13,650
Only the living.

255
00:21:18,930 --> 00:21:20,150
I know.

256
00:21:21,850 --> 00:21:23,280
But I still love her.

257
00:21:38,570 --> 00:21:40,500
You know nothing, Jon Snow.

258
00:22:18,280 --> 00:22:19,630
Are you lonely?

259
00:22:21,470 --> 00:22:22,470
Just bored.

260
00:22:22,470 --> 00:22:23,620
My father used to tell me

261
00:22:23,620 --> 00:22:26,270
that boredom indicates a lack of inner resources.

262
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:27,950
Were you bored a lot, too?

263
00:22:28,960 --> 00:22:31,630
I know Castle Black is no place for a child, but...

264
00:22:31,630 --> 00:22:32,800
I like it.

265
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:34,480
I thought I'd be left at home.

266
00:22:35,410 --> 00:22:37,280
I know mother didn't want to bring me.

267
00:22:38,300 --> 00:22:39,540
Why do you say that?

268
00:22:41,640 --> 00:22:43,580
She told me, "I don't want to bring you."

269
00:22:45,760 --> 00:22:47,230
She shouldn't have said that.

270
00:22:57,530 --> 00:22:59,250
Are you ashamed of me, father?

271
00:23:10,790 --> 00:23:12,250
When you were an infant,

272
00:23:13,410 --> 00:23:15,800
a Dornish trader landed on Dragonstone.

273
00:23:16,930 --> 00:23:20,220
His goods were junk except for one wooden doll.

274
00:23:21,610 --> 00:23:24,730
He had even sewn a dress on it in the colors of our House.

275
00:23:26,930 --> 00:23:28,950
No doubt he had heard of your birth

276
00:23:29,490 --> 00:23:32,350
and assumed new fathers were easy targets.

277
00:23:36,070 --> 00:23:39,320
I still remember how you smiled when I put that doll in your cradle.

278
00:23:40,870 --> 00:23:42,580
How you pressed it to your cheek.

279
00:23:50,310 --> 00:23:52,780
By the time we burnt the doll, it was too late.

280
00:23:55,710 --> 00:23:57,300
I was told you would die.

281
00:23:58,360 --> 00:23:59,610
Or worse.

282
00:24:01,050 --> 00:24:02,910
The greyscale would go slow.

283
00:24:03,430 --> 00:24:05,870
Let you grow just enough to know the world

284
00:24:05,870 --> 00:24:07,510
before taking it away from you.

285
00:24:08,090 --> 00:24:10,670
Everyone advised me to send you to the ruins of Valyria

286
00:24:10,670 --> 00:24:13,020
to live out your short life with the Stone men,

287
00:24:13,020 --> 00:24:15,360
before the sickness spread to the castle.

288
00:24:17,520 --> 00:24:19,330
I told them all to go to hell.

289
00:24:21,520 --> 00:24:24,360
I called in every maester on this side of the world.

290
00:24:24,360 --> 00:24:27,440
Every healer, every apothecary.

291
00:24:29,470 --> 00:24:31,850
They stopped the disease and saved your life.

292
00:24:33,140 --> 00:24:34,050
Because you did not belong

293
00:24:34,060 --> 00:24:36,200
across the world with the bloody Stone men.

294
00:24:38,050 --> 00:24:40,520
You are the Princess Shireen of House Baratheon.

295
00:24:43,130 --> 00:24:44,620
And you are my daughter.

296
00:25:46,680 --> 00:25:48,320
I thought I might find you here.

297
00:25:51,540 --> 00:25:52,910
Your Aunt Lyanna.

298
00:25:54,120 --> 00:25:55,990
Father never talked about her.

299
00:25:57,640 --> 00:26:00,640
Sometimes I'd find him down here lighting the candles.

300
00:26:02,320 --> 00:26:03,870
They say she was beautiful.

301
00:26:04,650 --> 00:26:06,090
I saw her once.

302
00:26:06,190 --> 00:26:08,540
I was a boy living with your mother's family.

303
00:26:09,470 --> 00:26:12,120
Lord Whent held a great tourney at Harrenhal.

304
00:26:13,440 --> 00:26:14,870
Everyone was there.

305
00:26:15,260 --> 00:26:16,620
The Mad King,

306
00:26:16,980 --> 00:26:18,260
your father,

307
00:26:18,570 --> 00:26:20,010
Robert Baratheon,

308
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:24,430
and Lyanna. She was already promised to Robert.

309
00:26:25,310 --> 00:26:28,100
You can imagine what it was like for me, a boy from nowhere

310
00:26:28,390 --> 00:26:29,800
with nothing to his name,

311
00:26:30,520 --> 00:26:34,090
watching these legendary men tilting at the lists.

312
00:26:35,300 --> 00:26:36,960
The last two riders were

313
00:26:36,960 --> 00:26:39,740
Barristan Selmy and Rhaegar Targaryen.

314
00:26:40,080 --> 00:26:43,280
When Rhaegar won, everyone cheered for their prince.

315
00:26:43,980 --> 00:26:44,900
I remember the girls laughing

316
00:26:44,900 --> 00:26:47,600
when he took off his helmet and they saw that silver hair.

317
00:26:48,060 --> 00:26:49,520
How handsome he was.

318
00:26:50,440 --> 00:26:54,700
Until he rode right past his wife, Elia Martell,

319
00:26:55,210 --> 00:26:56,920
and all the smiles died.

320
00:26:58,420 --> 00:27:00,710
I've never seen so many people so quiet.

321
00:27:02,010 --> 00:27:03,650
He rode past his wife

322
00:27:05,520 --> 00:27:08,600
and he lay a crown of winter roses in Lyanna's lap.

323
00:27:09,090 --> 00:27:10,710
Blue as frost.

324
00:27:14,850 --> 00:27:16,190
How many tens of thousands

325
00:27:16,190 --> 00:27:18,670
had to die because Rhaegar chose your aunt?

326
00:27:21,460 --> 00:27:23,280
Yes, he chose her.

327
00:27:24,330 --> 00:27:26,850
And then he kidnapped her and raped her.

328
00:27:35,020 --> 00:27:36,230
Come.

329
00:27:36,940 --> 00:27:39,270
Let's speak somewhere the dead can't hear us.

330
00:27:44,770 --> 00:27:47,070
- You're dressed for riding. - I am.

331
00:27:49,030 --> 00:27:50,340
Where are you going?

332
00:27:50,710 --> 00:27:52,030
King's Landing.

333
00:27:52,790 --> 00:27:54,110
King's Landing?

334
00:27:54,580 --> 00:27:56,050
Cersei sent for me.

335
00:27:56,690 --> 00:27:58,700
We must't let her sniff out any trouble.

336
00:27:59,390 --> 00:28:01,170
You can't leave me here.

337
00:28:01,170 --> 00:28:04,140
I know how hard it is to live with people you despise. Believe me.

338
00:28:05,170 --> 00:28:06,650
But it won't be for long.

339
00:28:07,230 --> 00:28:08,440
How do you know?

340
00:28:10,020 --> 00:28:12,790
Stannis Baratheon garrisons at Castle Black.

341
00:28:13,700 --> 00:28:15,460
He'll march south to King's Landing

342
00:28:15,460 --> 00:28:17,620
before the winter snows block his way.

343
00:28:17,620 --> 00:28:20,090
But first he has to take Winterfell.

344
00:28:21,010 --> 00:28:22,960
- You don't know that. - I do.

345
00:28:24,380 --> 00:28:26,500
Once he liberates these lands from the Boltons,

346
00:28:26,500 --> 00:28:28,830
he'll rally your father's bannermen to his cause.

347
00:28:29,010 --> 00:28:30,520
With the North behind him,

348
00:28:30,970 --> 00:28:33,210
Stannis can finally take the Iron Throne.

349
00:28:33,770 --> 00:28:35,690
You think he'll defeat the Boltons?

350
00:28:36,590 --> 00:28:38,040
He has a larger army.

351
00:28:38,170 --> 00:28:40,770
He's the finest military commander in Westeros.

352
00:28:40,840 --> 00:28:44,060
A betting man would put his money on Stannis.

353
00:28:44,650 --> 00:28:46,740
As it happens, I am a betting man.

354
00:28:48,390 --> 00:28:49,800
And if you're right?

355
00:28:50,150 --> 00:28:51,750
Stannis takes Winterfell,

356
00:28:52,270 --> 00:28:55,220
he rescues you from the most despised family in the North.

357
00:28:55,530 --> 00:28:58,520
Grateful for your late father's courageous support for his claim,

358
00:28:58,570 --> 00:29:00,920
he names you Wardeness of the North.

359
00:29:01,980 --> 00:29:04,440
But I-i wouldn't-

360
00:29:05,180 --> 00:29:06,520
wardeness of the North?

361
00:29:06,520 --> 00:29:08,700
You are the last surviving Stark.

362
00:29:09,490 --> 00:29:10,780
He needs you.

363
00:29:11,610 --> 00:29:12,380
And what if you're wrong?

364
00:29:12,380 --> 00:29:14,350
What if Stannis never attacks Winterfell?

365
00:29:14,350 --> 00:29:16,760
Or he does and the Boltons defeat him?

366
00:29:17,200 --> 00:29:19,290
Then you will take this Bolton boy, Ramsay,

367
00:29:19,300 --> 00:29:20,530
and make him yours.

368
00:29:21,480 --> 00:29:23,940
- I don't know how to do that. - Of course you do.

369
00:29:24,640 --> 00:29:26,360
He's already fallen for you.

370
00:29:27,120 --> 00:29:29,480
- His father frightens me. - He should.

371
00:29:29,480 --> 00:29:31,110
He's a dangerous man.

372
00:29:32,230 --> 00:29:35,150
But even the most dangerous men can be outmaneuvered.

373
00:29:36,080 --> 00:29:38,640
And you've learned to maneuver from the very best.

374
00:29:40,990 --> 00:29:42,790
I'll return before too long.

375
00:29:43,260 --> 00:29:45,140
You'll be strong without me.

376
00:29:54,180 --> 00:29:55,720
The North will be yours.

377
00:29:57,470 --> 00:29:58,740
Do you believe me?

378
00:30:01,660 --> 00:30:04,660
I expect I'll be a married woman by the time you return.

379
00:31:08,770 --> 00:31:09,980
Breakfast.

380
00:31:14,450 --> 00:31:16,220
That would have been a shit way to die.

381
00:31:16,270 --> 00:31:18,910
As far as I've seen, they're all shit ways to die.

382
00:31:19,490 --> 00:31:22,740
Aye, but your lot have to give the singers a good ending.

383
00:31:22,740 --> 00:31:25,050
I don't care what's sung about me when I'm dead.

384
00:31:25,640 --> 00:31:26,790
No?

385
00:31:27,470 --> 00:31:30,180
Two knights off to rescue a princess.

386
00:31:30,470 --> 00:31:33,770
- Sounds like a good song to me. - Sounds like all the rest.

387
00:31:37,250 --> 00:31:41,260
What about you? What shit way would you choose?

388
00:31:42,690 --> 00:31:45,510
In my own keep drinking my own wine

389
00:31:45,820 --> 00:31:48,190
watching my sons grovel for my fortune.

390
00:31:49,370 --> 00:31:50,840
How disappointing.

391
00:31:51,830 --> 00:31:54,020
I thought you'd have something more exciting planned.

392
00:31:55,210 --> 00:31:58,920
I've had an exciting life. I want my death to be boring.

393
00:32:01,090 --> 00:32:04,860
- How do you want to go? - In the arms of the woman I love.

394
00:32:08,780 --> 00:32:10,110
She want the same thing?

395
00:32:16,240 --> 00:32:17,310
Let's go.

396
00:32:27,750 --> 00:32:29,160
The captain to that ship...

397
00:32:29,740 --> 00:32:32,230
- what was he, Braavosi? - Pentoshi.

398
00:32:33,050 --> 00:32:34,570
And he's headed to Oldtown?

399
00:32:34,570 --> 00:32:35,800
As I said.

400
00:32:35,890 --> 00:32:37,080
Why?

401
00:32:37,360 --> 00:32:39,440
What's to stop him from docking down the coast

402
00:32:39,440 --> 00:32:42,180
and telling the locals that Jaime Lannister's in Dorne?

403
00:32:42,180 --> 00:32:43,520
A bag of gold.

404
00:32:44,520 --> 00:32:45,930
I'm not sure you understand

405
00:32:45,930 --> 00:32:48,710
how much people hate your family in this part of the world.

406
00:32:48,770 --> 00:32:50,130
It was a heavy bag.

407
00:32:50,610 --> 00:32:53,300
And I bet he swore all kinds of oaths to get it.

408
00:32:53,520 --> 00:32:55,770
But you won't be around if he breaks 'em.

409
00:33:05,440 --> 00:33:06,720
How many you count?

410
00:33:06,750 --> 00:33:07,870
Four.

411
00:33:08,090 --> 00:33:09,670
How many do you think you can take?

412
00:33:09,800 --> 00:33:11,780
One if he's slow.

413
00:33:15,560 --> 00:33:16,720
Halt!

414
00:33:17,390 --> 00:33:18,720
Over the hill.

415
00:33:21,430 --> 00:33:22,880
Fucked in the ass.

416
00:33:33,410 --> 00:33:34,580
Morning, lads.

417
00:33:36,030 --> 00:33:37,260
Glad we found you.

418
00:33:38,280 --> 00:33:39,480
Who are you?

419
00:33:39,810 --> 00:33:40,950
Cooper.

420
00:33:41,330 --> 00:33:42,660
This is Darnell.

421
00:33:42,990 --> 00:33:44,590
You're from King's Landing.

422
00:33:44,620 --> 00:33:45,990
Accent gave me away?

423
00:33:47,810 --> 00:33:48,880
Flea Bottom,

424
00:33:48,880 --> 00:33:50,110
whelped and whipped.

425
00:33:50,620 --> 00:33:51,710
Why are you here?

426
00:33:51,710 --> 00:33:53,530
Our ship capsized in the night.

427
00:33:53,530 --> 00:33:55,060
We managed to swim ashore.

428
00:33:55,870 --> 00:33:57,280
It was a near thing, really.

429
00:33:58,130 --> 00:33:59,920
I thought the sharks would get us.

430
00:34:01,250 --> 00:34:03,360
There are no sharks in Dorne.

431
00:34:04,890 --> 00:34:07,020
I could have sworn those were shark fins.

432
00:34:08,490 --> 00:34:09,820
Dolphins, maybe.

433
00:34:11,510 --> 00:34:13,120
Throw your swords in the sand.

434
00:34:13,580 --> 00:34:15,830
Boys, there's no need for this.

435
00:34:15,830 --> 00:34:18,530
Just point us in the right direction,

436
00:34:18,570 --> 00:34:20,140
we'll find our way home.

437
00:34:20,230 --> 00:34:21,730
Swords in the sand

438
00:34:21,830 --> 00:34:22,950
now!

439
00:34:50,350 --> 00:34:51,860
That one should be slow enough.

440
00:35:46,030 --> 00:35:47,140
Nice move!

441
00:35:49,440 --> 00:35:50,530
Luck.

442
00:35:51,450 --> 00:35:53,010
You had a wonderful teacher.

443
00:36:07,120 --> 00:36:09,090
Always wanted a Dornish stallion.

444
00:36:10,200 --> 00:36:13,110
Beasts can run a day and night without tiring.

445
00:36:13,850 --> 00:36:16,930
We'll ride to the Water Gardens with a nice breeze in our face.

446
00:36:16,930 --> 00:36:18,900
But first we need to bury these bodies.

447
00:36:19,730 --> 00:36:21,140
Birds have to eat, too.

448
00:36:21,150 --> 00:36:23,430
Corpses raise questions. Questions raise armies.

449
00:36:23,440 --> 00:36:25,050
We're not here to start a war.

450
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:28,640
Do you know how long it will take us to dig all those holes?

451
00:36:29,400 --> 00:36:31,800
I can't dig very well with one hand.

452
00:36:32,380 --> 00:36:33,810
Not at all, really.

453
00:37:04,880 --> 00:37:06,060
Mama...

454
00:37:12,580 --> 00:37:15,340
- Nym, Obara. - Will it be war?

455
00:37:15,540 --> 00:37:18,580
Prince Doran will weep for your father, but nothing else.

456
00:37:18,600 --> 00:37:20,770
We must avenge Oberyn ourselves.

457
00:37:21,140 --> 00:37:24,450
Without Doran, we have no army to march against the Lannisters.

458
00:37:25,160 --> 00:37:27,570
We don't need an army to start a war.

459
00:37:28,030 --> 00:37:31,240
Queen Cersei loves her children.

460
00:37:31,570 --> 00:37:33,090
And we have one of them.

461
00:37:33,090 --> 00:37:34,760
You may have a problem.

462
00:37:41,120 --> 00:37:43,240
A ship's captain who found me in Planky Town,

463
00:37:43,240 --> 00:37:45,430
claiming he had information to sell.

464
00:37:45,730 --> 00:37:49,070
He told me he smuggled Jaime Lannister into Dorne.

465
00:37:50,580 --> 00:37:52,100
He's come for Myrcella.

466
00:37:53,460 --> 00:37:55,250
If he gets to her before we do,

467
00:37:55,250 --> 00:37:57,620
we lose our only chance for revenge.

468
00:37:58,410 --> 00:38:00,050
You must choose.

469
00:38:01,180 --> 00:38:03,380
Doran's way and peace,

470
00:38:03,390 --> 00:38:04,530
or my way

471
00:38:05,030 --> 00:38:06,170
and war.

472
00:38:08,920 --> 00:38:10,970
I'm with you always.

473
00:38:11,870 --> 00:38:12,760
Nym?

474
00:38:17,860 --> 00:38:18,980
Obara?

475
00:38:20,470 --> 00:38:23,680
When I was a child, Oberyn came to take me to court.

476
00:38:24,290 --> 00:38:26,250
I had never seen this man, and yet

477
00:38:26,250 --> 00:38:28,390
he called himself my father.

478
00:38:28,790 --> 00:38:32,870
My mother wept, said I was too young and a girl.

479
00:38:35,650 --> 00:38:38,630
Oberyn tossed his spear at my feet and said

480
00:38:38,630 --> 00:38:41,580
"Girl or boy, we fight our battles,

481
00:38:41,580 --> 00:38:44,350
"but the gods let us choose our weapons."

482
00:38:44,910 --> 00:38:47,530
My father pointed to the spear

483
00:38:47,530 --> 00:38:49,830
and then to my mother's tears.

484
00:38:57,090 --> 00:38:58,980
I made my choice long ago.

485
00:39:02,320 --> 00:39:03,840
Will you untie me?

486
00:39:05,320 --> 00:39:07,340
Will you please untie me?

487
00:39:08,320 --> 00:39:09,640
Will you please?

488
00:39:33,220 --> 00:39:34,240
Thank you.

489
00:39:43,090 --> 00:39:44,240
Who are you?

490
00:39:44,840 --> 00:39:46,020
Your captor.

491
00:39:48,740 --> 00:39:49,950
Do you have wine?

492
00:39:50,220 --> 00:39:51,130
No.

493
00:39:52,460 --> 00:39:54,100
Can't sleep without wine.

494
00:39:54,100 --> 00:39:55,420
Then stay awake.

495
00:40:02,020 --> 00:40:03,280
You're going the wrong way.

496
00:40:05,070 --> 00:40:07,520
My sister is in Westeros.

497
00:40:07,520 --> 00:40:10,130
Westeros is west!

498
00:40:10,130 --> 00:40:11,450
We're heading east.

499
00:40:12,060 --> 00:40:13,880
I'm not taking you to your sister.

500
00:40:15,700 --> 00:40:17,860
You said you were taking me to the queen.

501
00:40:17,860 --> 00:40:18,860
I am.

502
00:40:19,140 --> 00:40:21,350
Queen Daenerys Targaryen.

503
00:40:21,350 --> 00:40:23,100
She's the queen I serve.

504
00:40:29,770 --> 00:40:31,890
What a waste of a good kidnapping.

505
00:40:33,100 --> 00:40:35,490
It so happens I was heading there myself.

506
00:40:35,490 --> 00:40:37,670
What business would you have with the queen?

507
00:40:37,670 --> 00:40:39,350
Gold and glory.

508
00:40:39,350 --> 00:40:40,620
Oh, and hate.

509
00:40:41,520 --> 00:40:43,860
If you'd ever met my sister, you'd understand.

510
00:40:45,050 --> 00:40:48,630
So, now that it's clear we're on the same side.

511
00:40:58,700 --> 00:41:01,580
A high born knight from the North of Westeros

512
00:41:01,580 --> 00:41:03,780
down on his luck in Essos.

513
00:41:04,540 --> 00:41:05,900
Dragon epaulets,

514
00:41:06,270 --> 00:41:08,310
bear sigil breast plate.

515
00:41:09,390 --> 00:41:11,090
You're Jorah Mormont.

516
00:41:12,820 --> 00:41:14,110
I have to ask.

517
00:41:14,510 --> 00:41:17,620
How exactly were you serving your queen in a whorehouse

518
00:41:17,620 --> 00:41:19,050
half a world away?

519
00:41:19,780 --> 00:41:22,250
Is it possible that you were running?

520
00:41:23,310 --> 00:41:25,080
Why would you be running?

521
00:41:25,080 --> 00:41:27,100
And why would she have sent you away?

522
00:41:28,020 --> 00:41:29,360
Oh, wait.

523
00:41:30,450 --> 00:41:32,840
You were spying on her, weren't you?

524
00:41:33,810 --> 00:41:35,500
It's all coming back to me.

525
00:41:35,500 --> 00:41:37,440
I was drunk through most of the small council meetings,

526
00:41:37,440 --> 00:41:39,210
but it's all coming back.

527
00:41:39,440 --> 00:41:42,540
You passed notes to Varys's little birds.

528
00:41:44,370 --> 00:41:46,170
She found out, didn't she?

529
00:41:46,810 --> 00:41:48,960
Found out and exiled you.

530
00:41:50,400 --> 00:41:53,650
Now you hope to win back her favor with a gift.

531
00:41:55,150 --> 00:41:56,470
Risky scheme.

532
00:41:57,510 --> 00:41:59,870
One might even say desperate.

533
00:42:01,560 --> 00:42:04,690
You think Daenerys will execute me and pardon you?

534
00:42:06,190 --> 00:42:08,460
I'd say the reverse is just as likely.

535
00:42:30,230 --> 00:42:32,280
Everyone looks happy enough from up here.

536
00:42:34,380 --> 00:42:35,280
What?

537
00:42:36,310 --> 00:42:38,660
I was thinking about all the times your brother

538
00:42:38,660 --> 00:42:40,420
made me go with him down from the Red Keep

539
00:42:40,420 --> 00:42:42,420
into the streets of King's Landing.

540
00:42:42,420 --> 00:42:44,930
- Why? - He liked to walk among the people.

541
00:42:44,930 --> 00:42:46,750
He liked to sing to them.

542
00:42:47,610 --> 00:42:49,790
- He sang to them? - Yes.

543
00:42:50,670 --> 00:42:53,420
Rhaegar would pick a spot on the Hook

544
00:42:53,420 --> 00:42:56,020
or the Street of Seeds and then he'd sing.

545
00:42:56,500 --> 00:42:58,050
Just like all the other minstrels.

546
00:42:58,050 --> 00:42:59,420
And what did you do?

547
00:42:59,420 --> 00:43:01,440
I made sure no one killed him.

548
00:43:01,450 --> 00:43:03,400
And I collected the money.

549
00:43:04,340 --> 00:43:06,480
What? He liked to see how much he could make.

550
00:43:06,480 --> 00:43:08,400
- He was good? - He was very good.

551
00:43:08,400 --> 00:43:09,720
Viserys never told you?

552
00:43:09,720 --> 00:43:12,230
He told me Rhaegar was good at killing people.

553
00:43:13,410 --> 00:43:15,150
Rhaegar never liked killing.

554
00:43:15,150 --> 00:43:16,320
He loved singing.

555
00:43:16,810 --> 00:43:18,360
And what did you do with the money?

556
00:43:18,360 --> 00:43:21,680
Well, one time, he gave it to the next minstrel down the street.

557
00:43:21,680 --> 00:43:24,390
One time, he gave it to an orphanage in Flea Bottom.

558
00:43:24,390 --> 00:43:25,530
One time,

559
00:43:26,440 --> 00:43:28,170
we got horribly drunk.

560
00:43:29,710 --> 00:43:30,690
Your Grace.

561
00:43:32,110 --> 00:43:35,220
Hizdahr is here, waiting in the audience chamber.

562
00:43:36,440 --> 00:43:38,220
How many others are there?

563
00:43:38,220 --> 00:43:40,280
Fifty? A hundred?

564
00:43:40,720 --> 00:43:42,530
Will you be joining us, Ser Barristan?

565
00:43:42,530 --> 00:43:46,090
I think I can protect you from Hizdahr zo Loraq.

566
00:43:46,090 --> 00:43:48,760
I think I can protect me from Hizdahr zo Loraq.

567
00:43:50,010 --> 00:43:51,660
Go, Ser Barristan.

568
00:43:51,660 --> 00:43:53,010
Sing a song for me.

569
00:43:53,600 --> 00:43:54,570
Your Grace.

570
00:44:00,300 --> 00:44:01,930
All men must die,

571
00:44:01,930 --> 00:44:04,610
- but not all can die in glory. - Glory?

572
00:44:04,610 --> 00:44:06,180
Why else do men fight?

573
00:44:06,180 --> 00:44:08,430
Why did your ancestors cross the Narrow Sea

574
00:44:08,430 --> 00:44:09,720
and conquer the Seven Kingdoms?

575
00:44:09,720 --> 00:44:11,840
So their names would live on.

576
00:44:12,260 --> 00:44:13,830
Those who find victory in the fighting pits

577
00:44:13,830 --> 00:44:15,100
will never become kings,

578
00:44:15,100 --> 00:44:17,230
but their names will live on.

579
00:44:17,490 --> 00:44:19,380
It's the best chance they'll ever have.

580
00:44:19,380 --> 00:44:20,510
Is that what you used to tell men

581
00:44:20,510 --> 00:44:23,750
before you set them to butchering each other for sport?

582
00:44:23,750 --> 00:44:26,610
Your Grace, today is the traditional start of the fighting season.

583
00:44:26,610 --> 00:44:28,360
I do not recognize this tradition.

584
00:44:28,360 --> 00:44:30,240
Traditions are the only thing

585
00:44:30,240 --> 00:44:33,390
that will hold this city, your city, together.

586
00:44:35,280 --> 00:44:38,810
Without them, former slaves and former masters have nothing in common.

587
00:44:40,650 --> 00:44:44,330
Nothing but centuries of mistrust and resentment.

588
00:44:45,090 --> 00:44:48,090
I can't promise this is the answer to all our problems,

589
00:44:49,130 --> 00:44:50,510
but it's a start.

